      "content": "i see. but \"dehumanization\" is such a subjective term though. some people argue that if a moderator flags a satirical joke just because it uses a certain word, they're actually suppressing political dissent and effectively silencing certain viewpoints. it feels like by prioritizing \"protection from harm\" over \"free expression,\" we might be setting a precedent that favors more mainstream/safe speech and penalizes anyone being edgy or unconventional. don't you think that approach inherently skews the platform's political landscape?",
